OL,3,GNEWSASchoolboys' 1850s copy of Bayeux
OL,4,ATapestry restored
OL,5,
OL,6,FA drawing copy of the Bayeux Tapestry,
OL,7,Fcreated in almost the same scale more
OL,8,Fthan 170 years ago, has been restored
OL,9,Fand put on display.
OL,11,FThe replica, based on the embroidered
OL,12,Fdepiction of the French invasion and
OL,13,Feventual conquest of England in 1066,
OL,14,Fis now being displayed at the Great
OL,15,FNorth Museum in Newcastle.
OL,17,FThe artefact was commissioned by a
OL,18,Fteacher named John Collingwood Bruce
OL,19,Fand created by schoolboys at his
OL,20,Fschool, Percy Street Academy in
OL,21,FNewcastle, in the early 1850s.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
